   "output": "Read only the page below. Read no other file, and do not run commands or browse. Answer each question from the page alone. When the page does not say, answer \"Not stated\".\n\n<<<PAGE\n# Renaming rooms in the Kestrel directory\n\n## 1. Identify a room by its key\n\nUse the room key to identify a room when you build a saved link. A rename changes the room\u2019s display name. Its key stays the same.\n\nKestrel is a fictional directory of shared work rooms. Each room has a room key and a display name. These values have different purposes:\n\n- The room key identifies the room. Kestrel assigns it when the room is created. It never changes or gets reused for another room.\n- The display name is the human-readable label people see. Room owners can change it.\n\nThis distinction lets a saved link continue to identify a room after its owner changes the label. When someone opens the link, Kestrel looks up the key and displays the room\u2019s current name. The name shown when the link opens can therefore differ from the name shown when it was saved.\n\nA link built from a display name can stop finding the room after a rename because that name has changed. Do not treat the display name as a permanent room identifier.\n\nIn the storage schema, `room_ref` is the key column and `title_text` is the display-name column. Keep these meanings clear when working with the stored values: `room_ref` identifies the room, while `title_text` supplies its human-readable label.\n\n## 2. Verify the rename with a saved link\n\nCheck a rename with a room link saved before the change. The expected result has two parts: the link reaches the same room, and Kestrel shows the new display name.\n\n1. Before renaming the room, save a link that identifies it by its room key.\n2. Have the room owner change the display name.\n3. Open the saved link.\n4. Confirm that it reaches the same room.\n5. Confirm that Kestrel displays the new name.\n\nSaving the link before the rename gives you a link from the room\u2019s earlier naming state. Opening that same link afterward checks that it still identifies the room.\n\nCheck both results separately. Reaching the same room verifies the saved link\u2019s target. Seeing the new name verifies that Kestrel displays the current label.\nPAGE>>>\n\nQuestions:\n(a) What stays the same when a room is renamed?\n(b) Can a link built from a display name stop working after a rename?\n(c) Which link should you open to verify that a rename preserved access?\n\nReply with only JSON: {\"a\": \"...\", \"b\": \"...\", \"c\": \"...\"}. Start the answer to (b) with Yes, No, or Not stated.",
